      "content": "thanks, that helps a lot. so if i'm looking at these two sides, it feels like the \"pro\" arguments are mostly about theoretical concepts like \"tyranny of the majority\" or \"state sovereignty,\" whereas the \"anti\" arguments are about how it actually affects real people's votes right now. is it fair to say the system is fundamentally broken if the practical reality doesn't match the original theoretical goal?",
